@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Image lineage — parent tags, ensure modes, and the publish contract

' purpose: which parent a child builds on, at which tag, and what the parent
'          ensure step actually checks in each of its two modes
' covers: internal/imagebuild/**
' covers: internal/imagetest/imagetest.go
' covers: internal/imagetest/detached_smoke_test.go
' covers: defs/sidecars/*/Dockerfile
' covers: internal/maintain/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintain_cmd.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/provision.go
' covers: internal/contract/image_resolution_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/import_boundary_test.go
' covers: lib/registry.sh
'
' ── EVERY TARGET HAS THE SAME SHAPE ─────────────────────────────────────────
' One row per registry target in internal/imagebuild/targets.go `Specs`; one
' entry point, Builder.BuildTarget(name, tag, Options{Push, NoCache}). The
' per-def build.sh/ensure.sh pairs and defs/lib/docker-build.sh held this shape
' until 2026-09-22 (_spec/_plans/host-shell-to-go.puml, P2).
'   ref = TargetRef(name, tag)   Spec.Repo, or RefRepo($PROVEO_<X>_IMAGE)
'                                the override names the REPO; --tag sets the tag
'   tag ""                       -> latest (and Build refuses latest for --load)
'   Options.NoCache              passed straight through as --no-cache
'   Options.Push                 switches every parent ensure into publication mode
'   RefTag(ref)                  the child's tag decides the parent's
'   ensure(Spec.Parent, ImageRef(Spec.ParentOverride, parent repo, tag), push)
'   Spec.Needs                   sibling built if missing; RequirePublished on push
'
' ── THE FLOOR PROBES, PER LAYER ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' A tag alone is not evidence: a stale image from a different lineage looks
' present and has the wrong contents. So ensure (targets.go) runs the parent
' row's Spec.Floor inside the image (`docker run --rm --entrypoint sh <ref> -c`),
' and the probe states the CONTRACT rather than restating the package list:
'
'   proveo/base            git · gh · jq · an executable
'                          /usr/local/bin/proveo-entrypoint. Explicitly no
'                          browser, no Node, no Python — those moved out.
'   proveo/base-node       git · jq · node · pnpm · bun · bunx · the entrypoint
'   proveo/base-node-lsp   node · jq · typescript-language-server ·
'                          pyright-langserver
'   proveo/base-node-browser  node · playwright · typescript-language-server ·
'                          a chromium-* dir under PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH ·
'                          agent-browser · an executable
'                          AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH · core/SKILL.md under
'                          AGENT_BROWSER_SKILLS_DIR ·
'                          /opt/proveo/skills/agent-browser/SKILL.md
'
' Probe fails on a PRESENT image -> rebuild from source. Image absent -> pull,
' then probe; pull failed or probe failed -> build from source. The messages name
' which of those three happened, because "missing the floor" and "not present"
' send a reader to different places. Spec.FloorWhat names the floor in each.
'
' ── BUILD CONTEXT IS NOT UNIFORM, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE ────────────────────
' Two groups, for one reason: does the Dockerfile COPY anything out of the repo?
'
'   Context "."      base (the Go builder copies cmd/ and internal/), cecli,
'                    cursor, opencode, codex, claudecode (both variants) — they
'                    COPY packages/lib, defs/subagents, defs/bridges, AGENTS.md.
'   Context <def>    base-node, base-node-lsp, base-node-browser — these COPY nothing
'               from the module (base-node-browser copies only its own skills/),
'               so the narrower context is free.
'
' A repo-root context is what makes the root .dockerignore load-bearing: without
' it, 201 MB of node_modules and .git reach the daemon on every harness build.
'
' A THIRD SHAPE, AND IT CONSTRAINS THE GO TREE. The sidecars build Go from a
' PARTIAL context: defs/sidecars/egress-proxy/Dockerfile copies go.mod, cmd/ and
' internal/ — no root-level .go files and no defs/ tree. So any package under
' internal/ that imports the ROOT package (where the embeds live) makes that
' image fail with "no required module provides package". The root package is for
' main packages to hand down: internal/manifest takes an fs.FS for exactly this
' reason, and internal/provider now does too. Two contract tests hold it — no
' internal package may import the root, and `go list -deps ./cmd/proveo-egress`
' must not reach it either, because enumerating deps is cheap and a full docker
' build is not. Neither existed when the bridge tables were first embedded.
'
' ── HELPERS WITH NON-OBVIOUS BODIES ─────────────────────────────────────────
' imagetest's `created` (internal/imagetest/imagetest.go) reads an image's build
' time for maintain.ResolveImage, the way posture's dockerImageCreated does for
' the runtime. docker reports RFC3339Nano ("2026-08-31T00:37:15.008872627Z"),
' which time.Parse accepts whole. Its shell predecessor, proveo_image_created in
' defs/lib/test-image.sh (deleted 2026-09-22, host-shell-to-go P3), had to trim
' the fraction and try GNU `date -u -d` then BSD `date -u -j -f`, because
' neither `date` accepts nanoseconds and the suites ran on Linux and macOS.
' `created` reports false when the host has no such image, which is what lets
' ResolveImage treat "absent" as "not a candidate" rather than as time zero.
'
' Builder.jsonField (imagebuild.go) reads one field path out of fetched JSON
' with encoding/json, so the host needs neither jq nor python3 (moved from
' _proveo_json_field in defs/lib/docker-build.sh 2026-09-22). A missing field
' yields "" — AgentVersion then reports the unresolved version by name rather
' than baking `@latest`.
'
' HostPlatform (imagebuild.go) maps runtime.GOARCH arm64 to linux/arm64 and
' everything else to linux/amd64 — QEMU and unusual hosts get the published
' default rather than an error.
'
' Only :latest is ever resolved by maintain.ResolveImage (and so by
' imagetest.Resolve). An explicit :v2 or a digest is a deliberate choice by the
' caller and is returned untouched.
'
' ── ONE RULE, IN ONE PLACE — AND THE SECOND OPINION IS BANNED ───────────────
' The detached smoke first named each image with a HARDCODED tag. `proveo build`
' tags a local build :local and only a publish moves :latest, so it smoke-tested
' a published artifact while reading as though it covered the build in the tree.
' Its fix then grew its own `for tag in local latest`, which prefers :local by
' EXISTENCE rather than by recency — a third answer to a question the codebase
' had settled twice. That is the shadow running the other way: a stale local
' build shadowed an image pulled a minute ago while the run read as coverage of
' the newer one. A second opinion about which image is current is worse than
' none, so TestNoAdHocLocalOverLatestResolvers refuses that loop in any .sh
' under defs/, e2e/ and scripts/.
' Since host-shell-to-go P3 the image suites hold ONE implementation: each names
' a repository and imagetest.Resolve calls maintain.ResolveImage per run
' (TestImageDetachedSmoke's smokeTargets carry no tag). The shell resolver and
' TestShellImageResolverMatchesResolveImage, the parity test that ran it and
' ResolveImage over one table, are deleted with it: one implementation cannot
' disagree with itself. TestImageSuitesResolveRatherThanPinThePublishTag now
' fails any line in internal/imagetest/*_test.go that names :latest outside
' imagetest.Resolve.

node "internal/imagebuild" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "ImageRef · TargetRef\n<override> <repo> <tag>" as REF <<app>>
  component "RefTag\n<ref> → tag (default latest)" as RTAG <<app>>
  component "ensure(Parent, ref, push)\ntargets.go" as ENSURE <<app>>
  component "RequirePublished\nregistry probe + advisory" as REQ <<app>>
}

folder "Lineage" as CHAIN <<host>> {
  component "proveo/base" as B <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node" as BN <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node-lsp" as BNL <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node-browser" as BNB <<app>>
  component "cecli · cursor" as H1 <<app>>
  component "opencode · claudecode · codex" as H2 <<app>>
  component "claudecode-solidity" as H3 <<app>>
}

node "Tag policy" as TAGS <<host>> {
  component "proveo build\n--load → :local (never :latest)" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "proveo deploy\nrequire :local → retag → --push" as DEPLOY <<app>>
  component "maintain.ResolveImage\nnewer of :local / :latest" as RESOLVE <<app>>
  component "imagetest.Resolve\ninternal/imagetest/imagetest.go" as SHRESOLVE <<app>>
}

node "internal/imagetest\n-tags=image suites" as DEFTESTS <<host>>

cloud "Registry" as REG <<cloud>>
component "A published image shadowing\nthe build under test" as SHADOW <<error>>
component "Unpublished parent\non a --push build" as FAIL <<error>>

B ARROW_MAIN BN
BN ARROW_MAIN BNL
BNL ARROW_MAIN BNB
B ARROW_MAIN H1
BNL ARROW_MAIN H2
H2 ARROW_MAIN H3

REF ARROW_MAIN CHAIN : every ""BASE_IMAGE"" at the CHILD'S tag
RTAG ARROW_MAIN REF : derive the tag from the image being built
ENSURE ARROW_MAIN CHAIN : local — present · floor · pull · build
ENSURE ARROW_CLOUD REQ : ""--push"" — publication is all that matters
REQ ARROW_CLOUD REG : ""buildx imagetools inspect""
REQ ARROW_ERROR FAIL : fail early, at the declaration site
BUILD ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE : ""<image>:local""
BUILD ARROW_MAIN DEPLOY : the tested image
DEPLOY ARROW_CLOUD REG : promoted, multi-arch
RESOLVE ARROW_ERROR SHADOW : prevented by tag, not by luck
REG ARROW_ERROR SHADOW : sbx re-pulls at sandbox creation
DEFTESTS ARROW_MAIN SHRESOLVE : resolve before the first ""docker run""
SHRESOLVE ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE : calls it — one implementation

note right of REF
  **A child never hardcodes ""latest"".** Every parent reference is
  resolved through ""ImageRef"", so ""proveo deploy all --tag v2""
  publishes ""proveo/<harness>:v2"" built ""FROM proveo/base:v2"". Left
  hardcoded, the published lineage silently mixes two releases and
  nothing in the image records it.

  A PARENT's ""PROVEO_*_IMAGE"" override wins outright — it is a
  complete ref chosen by the caller, so the tag is not reapplied to it.
  The TARGET's own override names only its repo: ""TargetRef"" applies
  ""--tag"" to it, so ""proveo build"" still writes ""<repo>:local"".
end note

note bottom of ENSURE
  **The two modes answer different questions.**

  ""--tag"" (local ""--load""): is the parent present at this tag with a
  usable floor? Present + floor → done; else pull; else build from
  source. A tag alone is not enough — a stale image from a different
  lineage looks present but has the wrong contents, so ensure runs
  the row's ""Spec.Floor"" probe (the tools that layer must provide).

  ""--push"": the child resolves the parent from the REGISTRY, so the
  local pull/floor dance answers the wrong question entirely and is
  skipped. Only publication matters.
end note

note bottom of REQ
  **Deploying one target whose parents are unpublished is not
  supported.** ""RequirePublished"" refuses to publish a parent as a side effect
  of a child's deploy — that would push an image the caller never
  asked for, and (for claudecode-solidity) a local ""docker image
  inspect"" would be interrogating the wrong store while the build
  resolves from the registry.

  Failing at the declaration site turns a bare 'failed to resolve
  source metadata … not found' 30 seconds into the build into an
  actionable message naming ""proveo deploy all"" and the parent target.
end note

note right of CHAIN
  **Each layer exists where it does so its consumers can decline it.**

  | layer | holds | why not lower |
  | ""proveo/base"" | git · gh · ca-certs · curl · jq · dumb-init · bash · tmux · ""proveo-entrypoint"" · the harden pass | the universally-shared floor, and **no language runtime** |
  | ""proveo/base-node"" | Node + pnpm + Bun | cursor and cecli would otherwise carry a Node runtime they never call |
  | ""proveo/base-node-lsp"" | the language servers ""_lsp_server()"" can run | a non-LSP Node consumer should not pay for them |
  | ""proveo/base-node-browser"" | Playwright + Chromium + agent-browser, chromium library set | ``-browser`` variants apply this file onto the harness |
  | ""claudecode-solidity"" | Foundry · solc-select · solhint · semgrep | ~1.5 GB of toolchain, on the one harness that audits contracts |

  **Two size lessons are baked into the shape.** The Solidity toolchain was
  split out because it alone doubled the harness image; and its per-user
  toolchains are installed **once, as the runtime user** — the earlier
  root-install-then-copy-to-home pattern shipped the 400 MB toolkit twice
  in one image.

  **The browser layer pins Playwright deliberately.** CLI, driver and the
  installed browser must move together — a mismatch surfaces as "can't
  locate browser executables" rather than as a version error. The browser
  store is shared and world-readable because the harness never runs as
  root: an arbitrary run-as uid has to be able to launch Chromium, and a
  repo-local Playwright honours the same variable, so a project's own
  ""npx playwright install"" lands in the same place. agent-browser is
  pinned the same way (version + tarball digest) and pointed at that
  store through a revision-stable symlink, so the layer holds ONE
  Chromium for two clients (_spec/defs/browser-layer.puml).

  Every layer that runs apt or npm re-runs the harden pass over the
  prefixes it touched, because a new package can reintroduce a setuid
  binary.
end note


note bottom of CHAIN
  **""proveo deploy all"" is the coherent publish path.** The maintainer
  registry is hand-ordered bases-first, then harnesses alphabetically,
  so every parent is published before its children — including
  claudecode before claudecode-solidity. Alphabetical order satisfying
  that last pair is a coincidence, not a declared edge.

  ""runPlan"" stops at the first failure, so a mid-fleet failure leaves a
  partially published set.
end note
note bottom of ENSURE
  **Every target is one ""Specs"" row, and the chain is what makes a single
  build work from cold.** ""BuildTarget"" builds exactly its own image and
  ensures its ""Parent"" first; that parent's build in turn ensures its own.
  So building any harness from a clean machine walks the lineage upward
  once, and no row needs to know the whole chain — only its immediate
  parent. ""TestEverySpecIsARegistryTarget"" pins the table to the registry.

  Build context (""Spec.Context"") follows what the Dockerfile COPIES. The
  harnesses and ""base"" use the REPO ROOT, because they resolve
  ""packages/lib"", ""defs/subagents"", ""defs/bridges"", ""AGENTS\.md"" and (for
  ""base"") ""cmd""/""internal"" from there. ""base-node"", ""base-node-lsp"" and
  ""base-node-browser"" pass their own directory: they copy nothing out of the
  module, so the narrow context costs them nothing and hands the daemon far
  less. The root ""\.dockerignore"" is what keeps the wide case honest.
end note


note top of BUILD
  **A local build never writes ""latest"".** That
  tag means published, and while one name covered
  both, anything re-resolving the reference could
  serve the registry artifact over the build under
  test, with nothing recording which one ran.
end note

note bottom of DEPLOY
  **Deploy promotes; it never builds blind.** It
  requires ""<image>:local"" and retags that image
  before pushing, so publishing without a local
  build refuses rather than shipping something
  nothing was ever run against.
end note

note top of RESOLVE
  **Recency decides, not existence.** A stale
  local image must not shadow one just pulled, and
  a build from a minute ago must not lose to the
  registry, so the runtime compares build times
  and names which image actually won.
end note

note bottom of SHADOW
  **The sandbox backend re-pulls by reference.**
  sbx resolves the image at creation and takes it
  from the registry, so a week-old published tag
  reached the container while every local rebuild
  appeared to succeed and changed nothing.
end note

note bottom of SHRESOLVE
  **The def suites had the shadow the runtime was spared.** Every
  ""test\.sh"" and ""tests/helpers\.sh"" defaulted to ""<image>:latest"" —
  a tag ""Builder.Build"" REFUSES to write locally — so the only
  image they could ever reach was whatever the registry last
  published. ""mise run test-images"" read as a verdict on the working
  tree and was a verdict on the last deploy.

  Measured: ""defs/cecli/test\.sh"" failed
  ""proveo\.agent\.version label missing"" against a ""proveo/cecli:latest""
  pulled from the registry, built 2026-08-31 — three days before the
  label was added to the Dockerfile. The suite was right, the image
  was old, and nothing on the path could have produced a newer one.

  Ten sites carried it (four harnesses, their browser and solidity
  variants, the mitmproxy sidecar). They shared a shell resolver until
  2026-09-22; the Go suites now call ""imagetest\.Resolve"", and
  ""imagetest\.New"" logs the image it chose — because an image silently
  resolving to a published artifact is invisible until something
  behaves like code nobody wrote. ""TargetRef"" keeps its ""latest"" default for an empty
  tag: publishing (""--push"") is what that tag is for.
end note

@enduml
